.TH VM-CONFIG 5 "2026" "vm-manager" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
vm-config \- configuration file for vm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vm/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
The optional TOML configuration file for
.BR vm (1),
at
.I ~/.config/vm/config.toml
when
.I XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset. Omitted settings take their defaults. An unreadable file, invalid
TOML or an unknown setting is an error.
.PP
.B vm config
shows the file and its defaults, and changes it; see
.BR vm (1).
.SH CATALOGUES
Images are named by catalogues. Remote catalogues are fetched by
.BR "vm update" ;
local catalogues are read where they are. Where catalogues name the same image,
the later one wins: remotes in the order given, then locals in the order given,
then
.BR store ,
the local catalogue
.B vm clone
and
.B vm import
write to. A name used twice within one catalogue is an error.
.TP
.B [[remote]]
A remote catalogue.
.B name
(lowercase letters, digits and dashes) identifies it;
.B url
names a pointer file;
.B path
is the directory holding the entries within the archive's top-level directory,
default
.BR catalogue .
Without any
.BR [[remote]] ,
the project's catalogue at vm\-manager.com is the one remote, named
.BR project .
.IP
The pointer file sets
.BR version ,
the catalogue's version, and
.BR archive ,
its gzipped tar archive: an http or https URL, or a file name resolved beside
the pointer.
.TP
.B [[local]]
A local catalogue:
.B name
as for a remote, and
.BR path ,
an absolute directory of entries.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.BR auto_pull " (boolean)"
Whether
.B vm run
fetches an image that is not held. Default
.BR true .
When
.BR false ,
a missing image is an error unless
.B \-\-pull
says otherwise.
.TP
.BR add_ssh_config " (boolean)"
Whether
.B vm run
acts as though
.B \-\-add\-ssh\-config
were given. Default
.BR false .
Images without cloud-init get no entry, and
.B \-\-no\-ssh\-config
overrides it. Existing machines are unaffected; use
.B vm start
to change them.
.TP
.BR default_user " (string)"
The account
.B vm run
creates when
.B \-\-user
is not given. The value
.B $USER
means the login name of the user running
.BR vm .
Default
.BR vm .
.SH EXAMPLE
.RS
.nf
auto_pull = false
add_ssh_config = true
default_user = "$USER"

[[remote]]
name = "project"
url = "https://vm\-manager.com/catalogue.toml"

[[remote]]
name = "internal"
url = "https://mirror.example.com/vm/catalogue.toml"
path = "images"

[[local]]
name = "team"
path = "/srv/vm/catalogue"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vm (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
